# L §8 Refusals outrank holes, L §8.1 "It stops propagating" (tally 2.1.8 R11, #169-a; T's fixes/g6/r4_d2): x / 0 is
# refused whatever x is, so with x a hole the outcome is decided without it: RUN-DIV, plainly (d) and under partial (p).
# Its twin x / two stays the hole (h). 2.1.7's refcore printed the hole ?"x?" (x) for d.
=== m.tally
model m
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
input x: num question "x?"
input zero: num
input two: num

ask d: x / zero
ask p: x / zero partial
ask h: x / two

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  x = ? "unknown"
  zero = 0 "s"
  two = 2 "s"
=== expect
d: refused: RUN-DIV division by zero
  cut 2026-01-01
h: ?"unknown" (x)
  cut 2026-01-01
p: refused: RUN-DIV division by zero
  cut 2026-01-01
